> Converted from personal notes. Amounts are for one serving. Directions are editorial, not verified source instructions.

> REVIEW: Range 1/5 to 2/5: upper amount 2/5 selected for shopping.

> Additional source: https://mykoreankitchen.com/wprm_print/spicy-gochujang-mayo

== Ingredients ==

Gather the following ingredients: @ground beef{3/10%lb}, @gluten-free panko breadcrumbs{1/10%cup}, @egg{1/5}, @green onions{3/5} (finely sliced), @garlic cloves{3/5} (minced), @ginger{1/5%tbsp} (grated), @gluten-free tamari{2/5%tbsp}, @gluten-free gochujang{1/5%tbsp}, @brown sugar{2/5%tbsp}, @sesame oil{2/5%tsp}, @black pepper{1/10%tsp}, @gluten-free mayo{1/10%cup}, @gluten-free sriracha{2/5%tbsp}, @rice vinegar or lime juice{1/5%tbsp}, @sesame seeds{2/5%tsp}, @green onions{2/5} (sliced).

== Preparation ==

Combine beef, breadcrumbs, egg and some of the aromatics; shape into meatballs and bake until fully cooked. Prepare a glaze with tamari, gochujang, sugar, sesame oil and remaining aromatics. Coat the meatballs. Mix mayonnaise, sriracha and vinegar or lime for dipping and garnish with sesame and green onion.
